## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to implement a cross-topic enrichment pattern with per-key state management, handle late-arriving data, and ensure at-least-once semantics with idempotent outputs.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-topic join by userId
- Windowing: 5-minute hopping window with 2-minute late-arrival tolerance
- Per-key state store with TTL-based eviction
- Idempotent outputs to prevent duplicates across restarts
- EnrichmentStore API exposure for testing and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
class CrossTopicEnrichmentSink {
  constructor(windowSize = 5 * 60 * 1000, lateTolerance = 2 * 60 * 1000) {
    this.store = new Map();
    this.emittedKeys = new Set();
    this.windowSize = windowSize;
    this.lateTolerance = lateTolerance;
  }

  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    const { topic, userId, timestamp, data } = msg;
    const key = `${topic}:${userId}:${this.getWindowId(timestamp)}`;

    if (this.emittedKeys.has(key)) return;

    if (!this.store.has(userId)) {
      this.store.set(userId, { clicks: [], impressions: [], firstSeen: Date.now() });
    }

    const buffer = this.store.get(userId);
    buffer[topic].push({ ...data, timestamp });

    this.tryEnrich(userId, key);
  }

  tryEnrich(userId, key) {
    const buffer = this.store.get(userId);
    if (buffer.clicks.length > 0 && buffer.impressions.length > 0) {
      const enriched = {
        userId,
        clicks: buffer.clicks,
        impressions: buffer.impressions,
        enrichedAt: Date.now()
      };
      this.emittedKeys.add(key);
      buffer.clicks = [];
      buffer.impressions = [];
      return enriched;
    }
  }

  getWindowId(timestamp) {
    return Math.floor(timestamp / this.windowSize);
  }

  commitOffsets() {
    this.emittedKeys.clear();
  }

  enrichmentStore() {
    return this.store;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

To test understanding of consumer rebalances and offset management, a common pitfall for beginners where duplicates occur if offsets aren't tracked during rebalances.

## Key Concepts

- Consumer group rebalancing
- Per-topic offset tracking
- In-flight state
- Safe commit on revoke
- Timeouts and fault tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo code showing API hooks
class RebalanceSafeConsumer {
  constructor() { this.committedOffsets = new Map(); this.inFlight = new Set(); }
  onPartitionsAssigned(parts) { for (const p of parts) { const k = `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`; const start = (this.committedOffsets.get(k) ?? -1) + 1; this.seek(p.topic, p.partition, start); } }
  onPartitionsRevoked(parts) { const revoked = new Set(parts.map(p => `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`)); /* wait for inFlight on revoked before committing */ }
  processMessage(msg) { const id = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}:${msg.offset}`; this.inFlight.add(id); // downstream write then:
    this.inFlight.delete(id); const key = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}`; this.committedOffsets.set(key, msg.offset); }
  commitOffsets() { /* commit logic here */ }
}
```

